reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 is identified by "https://system.org/example#REG2025202ART1_Rule1".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 is a prescriptive rule.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 has the label "Regulation 2025/202, Article 1, rule 1".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 has the modality permission.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/202/art_1/2025-11-01".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 produces reg 2025202 art 1 action 1.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 1 has the legal text "By way of further derogation from paragraph 3, point (d), the Member State concerned may allow fishing for European eel of an overall length of 12 cm or more when migrating from Union waters to their spawning grounds in the Sargasso Sea (downstream migration) for up to a total of 50 consecutive or non-consecutive days.".


reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 is identified by "https://system.org/example#REG2025202ART1_Rule2".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 is a prescriptive rule.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 has the label "Regulation 2025/202, Article 1, rule 2".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 has the modality obligation.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/202/art_1/2025-11-01".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 produces reg 2025202 art 1 action 2.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 2 has the legal text "That shall apply to all fishers concerned in the relevant fishing area, during the main migration period, under the following cumulative conditions".


reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 is identified by "https://system.org/example#REG2025202ART1_Rule3".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 is a prescriptive rule.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 has the label "Regulation 2025/202, Article 1, rule 3".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 has the modality obligation.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/202/art_1/2025-11-01".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 produces reg 2025202 art 1 action 3.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 3 has the legal text "such fishing activity shall only be allowed when the only access to marine waters necessarily passes through non-Union brackish waters.".


reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 is identified by "https://system.org/example#REG2025202ART1_Rule4".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 is a prescriptive rule.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 has the label "Regulation 2025/202, Article 1, rule 4".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 has the modality obligation.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/202/art_1/2025-11-01".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 produces reg 2025202 art 1 action 4.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 4 has the legal text "the catches taken in ICES subdivisions 22-32 shall meet the minimum conservation reference size of 35 cm, in accordance with Annex VIII, Part A, to Regulation (EU) 2019/1241 of the European Parliament and of the Council.".


reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 is identified by "https://system.org/example#REG2025202ART1_Rule5".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 is a prescriptive rule.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 has the label "Regulation 2025/202, Article 1, rule 5".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 has the modality prohibition.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/202/art_1/2025-11-01".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 produces reg 2025202 art 1 action 5.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 5 has the legal text "any eel that is sexually mature and is caught shall not be harmed, shall be transported without undue delay and shall be immediately released to nearby Union marine waters at a place designated by the Member State concerned, which would allow them to continue downstream migration.".


reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 is identified by "https://system.org/example#REG2025202ART1_Rule6".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 is a prescriptive rule.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 has the label "Regulation 2025/202, Article 1, rule 6".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 has the modality prohibition.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/202/art_1/2025-11-01".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 produces reg 2025202 art 1 action 6.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 6 has the legal text "any incidentally by-caught eel that is not sexually mature shall not be harmed and shall be immediately released back into the water.".


reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 is identified by "https://system.org/example#REG2025202ART1_Rule7".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 is a prescriptive rule.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 has the label "Regulation 2025/202, Article 1, rule 7".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 has the modality obligation.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/202/art_1/2025-11-01".

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 produces reg 2025202 art 1 action 7.

reg 2025202 art 1 rule 7 has the legal text "the fishing activity shall be undertaken with the involvement of a national scientific body.".


